WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.210
SPEAKER: Let's deploy an ASP.NET
Core app to Google App Engine.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.830
Inside Cloud Shell, create a
hello world ASP.NET Core web

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:12.812
app.

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:15.720
Restore the
dependencies of the app,

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.510
and publish to get a
self-contained DLL.

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:21.900
Now let's create a Docker file
inside the Publish folder.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.570
Docker file builds on the
official Google App Engine

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:29.390
image for ASP.NET Core 1.1 apps.

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:33.690
Next, create an app YAML
file for App Engine.

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:37.780
And finally, deploy to App
Engine using gcloud app deploy.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.910
In a few minutes,
your app is deployed

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:49.200
and running on App Engine.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:58.000
Thanks for watching.

